{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxzixiyWrc3xmsjoy92n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every day, the sea rises and falls along the world's coastlines, and for most of human history the reason was a mystery. Today we know that tides are the product of gravity. The Moon's gravitational pull stretches the Earth's oceans toward it, creating a bulge of water on the side facing the Moon. A second bulge forms on the opposite side, where the Moon's pull on the solid Earth is strongest relative to the water. As the planet rotates beneath these two bulges, most coastal locations pass through them roughly twice a day, producing the familiar rhythm of high and low tide.\n\nThe pattern is more complicated than a simple two-bulge model suggests. The Sun exerts its own tidal force, about half as strong as the Moon's despite its far greater mass, because it is so much farther away. When the Sun and Moon align at new or full moon, their effects combine into spring tides, which bring the highest high waters and lowest low waters. When they pull at right angles, during the quarter moons, their effects partly cancel, producing smaller neap tides.\n\nLocal geography then shapes what reaches the shore. Deep open ocean sees tides of only a metre or so, but narrow bays, funnel-shaped estuaries, and continental shelves can amplify them dramatically. The Bay of Fundy in Canada regularly experiences ranges above 15 metres, among the largest on Earth. Tides also drive currents, mix nutrient-rich water into shallow seas, and shape intertidal ecosystems where organisms must survive repeated exposure to air and submersion.\n\nTides have shaped human life for millennia. Sailors timed harbour entries around them, and tidal power harnesses this energy in estuaries and straits. Tides reshape Earth: friction moves energy from Earth's rotation to the Moon, lengthening our day by about 2.3 milliseconds per century."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14739,"cache_read_input_tokens":11228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14739},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18882075-b7e5-4411-9847-43c1c56c7340","uuid":"ff8840ff-4736-49b0-8a86-a7e1b7ef91ee","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:45:21.484Z","request_id":"req_011CfxzixMthbjLG5F8icLSS"}
